WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.124
The response has to be exercised,

2
00:00:02.124 --> 00:00:06.425
and Learn sets the rules in its
tutorial on DDoS simulation testing.

3
00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:11.289
Simulations run only through
Microsoft's approved partners, MazeBolt,

4
00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:16.730
Red Button and RedWolf, only against the
agency's own protected Azure public I Ps,

5
00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.863
and preferably in staging
or off-peak windows.

6
00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:24.300
Before the exercise, write the response
team and runbook that Learn's page on

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.595
securing a DDoS deployment recommends,
including how to raise a severity

8
00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:32.750
A support request to the Rapid Response
team under Network Protection.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.592
The exercise proves three things the
guide's Validate step asks for: the alert

10
00:00:37.592 --> 00:00:40.769
fired, the action group
paged the security monitor,

11
00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:42.812
and the logs show the mitigation.

12
00:00:42.812 --> 00:00:47.307
The rollout itself is gentle:
one non-production network first,

13
00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:51.715
the policy in audit for an evaluation
cycle, then rings, the hub,

14
00:00:51.715 --> 00:00:57.140
then Online and Corp landing zones, and
only then the policy's Modify effect.
